{
 "version": 1,
 "seed": 10,
 "name": "16. DVD anime",
 "description": "LR made the way an anime DVD is: mastered down to an anamorphic NTSC or PAL frame (NTSC discs mostly 3:2 pulled down) with mild halos, MPEG-2 encoded with DVD settings, then decoded, badly de-telecined, smoothed and scaled up by a player. HR is the clean Blu-ray. Grain is added to LR only, so the model learns to remove it; move Film Grain in front of Split into Chunks to keep grain in both.",
 "summary": "Blu-ray anime to DVD-quality LR",
